      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While you're right that powerful nations often leverage these organizations to impose their will, dismissing them as mere relics overlooks their critical role in enforcing the specific norms and \"red lines\" that allow great powers to act with relative impunity. These bodies function effectively as a necessary counterweight to unchecked unilateralism, forcing superpowers to compromise their immediate interests to maintain a fragile global order. Without such mechanisms, the strategic advantage of concentrated power would inevitably lead to a toxic environment where every state feels pressured to preemptively dismember rivals.",
